{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068994-life-arcana-and-animal-forms","id":1068994,"title":"Life Arcana and Animal Forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-27T19:48:57-07:00","id":1068994,"title":"Life Arcana and Animal Forms","content":"Is there a consolidated resource outlining a broad range of animal stats for people with Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, beyond the bat/cat/dog/horse/raven samples in the WoD core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T22:45:27-07:00","id":1069126,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/816385-official-chronicles-of-darkness-resources-faq-animal-stats-condition-and-power-cards\">Chronicles of Darkness General</a> forum. Or <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">direct link</a> to the Google doc with stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11760-tauspher","name":"Tauspher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T11:09:32-07:00","id":1069479,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much! Those stat blocks are varied enough that it shouldn't be hard to add more specific species to it, or apply the stat block to a new, but similar form.<br /> <br /> Life 4 would otherwise be potentially Very confusing without a clear list.<br /> <br /> Slightly related question: The Life 4 rote <i>Doppleganger</i> allows the mage to bodily transform into other people, but does Not adopt their physical traits like when said mage uses the Life 4 rote <i>Shapechanging</i> unless they also use <i>Supreme Honing </i>as well. If the mage can turn into something as massive as a blue whale (complete with with stat mods), then why not a normal human (non-supernatural) form? Of course, this is a 1-E question... I don't know if this was changed in 2-E or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:43:31-07:00","id":1069547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068994-life-arcana-and-animal-forms?p=1069479#post1069479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly related question: The Life 4 rote <i>Doppleganger</i> allows the mage to bodily transform into other people, but does Not adopt their physical traits like when said mage uses the Life 4 rote <i>Shapechanging</i> unless they also use <i>Supreme Honing </i>as well. If the mage can turn into something as massive as a blue whale (complete with with stat mods), then why not a normal human (non-supernatural) form? Of course, this is a 1-E question... I don't know if this was changed in 2-E or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Doppleganger </i>isn't in the 2E corebook, but <i>Mutable Mask</i> is a 2 dot spell that allows you to make superficial changes, with a Reach you can copy specific people. Still no Attribute changes there. But <i>Many Faces</i> is a 3-dot spell that references Mutable Mask but does not specify about specific people or not ( I think I'd allow it with a Reach still). It does allow you to rearrange physical attribute dots, but not increase above the total or reduce any one to 0. <i>Shapechanging </i>is 4-dots and says it lets you wholly take on the form a of a new creature, I'd allow that to be another, stronger Human, again with Reach to be a specific Human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Decided I'd require a Reach for the last bit. 03-28-2017, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}